invariant: INV-53
file: test/violations.py
catches: test/lint-matrix.sh
reason: shard_of drops the last names of a set whose size N does not
  divide, so a sharded job never checks them. Before the five INV-53
  files, each selection held a multiple of 4 violations, and a check of
  those sets alone passed this edit. So lint-matrix also checks shard_of
  over lists of every length from N to 3N.

--- old
    k, n = int(match.group(1)), int(match.group(2))
    return sorted(names)[k - 1::n]
--- new
    k, n = int(match.group(1)), int(match.group(2))
    names = sorted(names)
    return names[k - 1:len(names) - len(names) % n:n]
